<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Device framework compatibility matrix for Motorola SM8635 (arcfox).

     GENERATED. Every entry is optional="true": these are vendor HALs the stock
     image provides and which no AOSP framework compatibility matrix knows about.
     Without them the build fails at check_vintf_compatible with
       "ERROR: files are incompatible: The following instances are in the device
        manifest but not specified in framework compatibility matrix:"
     followed by the list this file is generated from.

     REGENERATE, do not hand-edit, whenever the vendor manifest gains a HAL:
       scratchpad/genmatrix.py  (merges this file with the current failure list)
     The merge matters. checkvintf only lists instances that are NOT yet covered,
     so regenerating from the failure list ALONE silently drops every entry that
     is currently doing its job, and the next build fails with those instead.

     History: first generated 2026-08-07 with 26 entries. Regenerated 2026-08-10
     after restoring further vendor blobs grew the manifest; the stale file was
     only noticed because adding a VINTF fragment invalidated a check_vintf
     result that had been cached since 2026-08-07. -->
